---
import FieldGuideLayout from '../../../components/FieldGuideLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<FieldGuideLayout
  title="RESC container (version 3.11)"
  description="Konami's named-entry archive. 48-byte TOC entries with two reversed-ASCII names. Used by item/itemslot.lzs and item/ItemEtc.lzs."
  crumbs={[
    { label: 'Field Guide', href: `${base}/field-guide/` },
    { label: 'File Formats', href: `${base}/field-guide/file-formats/` },
    { label: 'RESC' },
  ]}
>
  <p>
    Variant of <a href={`${base}/field-guide/file-formats/reso/`}>RESO</a> that
    stores named TOC entries instead of type tags. Each entry is 48 bytes.
  </p>

  <h2>Header (16 bytes)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th><th>Value</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>0x00</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>magic</td><td><code>"RESC"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x04</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32 LE</code></td><td>file_count</td><td>Number of TOC entries</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x08</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>version</td><td>Typically <code>"3.11"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>0x0C</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32 LE</code></td><td>variant / flags</td><td>(observed 0)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>TOC entry (48 bytes)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Offset</th><th>Size</th><th>Type</th><th>Field</th><th>Notes</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>+0x00</code></td><td>16</td><td><code>char[16]</code></td><td>name1</td><td>Reversed ASCII; e.g. <code>"u_gak_noci"</code> → <code>"icon_kag_u"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x10</code></td><td>16</td><td><code>char[16]</code></td><td>name2</td><td>Reversed ASCII; e.g. <code>"rgcn"</code> → <code>"ncgr"</code></td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x20</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32 LE</code></td><td>unk</td><td>Often 0</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x24</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>char[4]</code></td><td>type_tag</td><td>Reversed ASCII (same encoding as RESO)</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x28</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32 LE</code></td><td>length</td><td>Payload bytes</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>+0x2C</code></td><td>4</td><td><code>u32 LE</code></td><td>data_offset</td><td>Absolute offset within file</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Where RESC appears</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>item/itemslot.lzs</code> — item-slot metadata.</li>
    <li><code>item/ItemEtc.lzs</code> — additional item attributes.</li>
    <li>About 70 compressed files, mostly under
      <code>data/2d/solvedeventlist/</code>, plus a few other one-off
      containers.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Decoder behavior</h2>
  <p>
    The project's <code>_sprite_assoc.py</code> does not currently decode RESC
    names; for the palette-association table RESC is treated as
    RESO-equivalent (TOC entries indexed by position, payloads sliced by
    <code>(length, data_offset)</code>). Names are useful for reading
    intent — <code>"icon_kag_u"</code> identifies an item-icon group — but
    are not required for asset extraction.
  </p>

  <h2>Annotated hex dump (truncated)</h2>
  <pre><code>{`offs  bytes                                              meaning
----  -------------------------------------------------- --------------------------------
0000  52 45 53 43                                        magic = "RESC"
0004  XX 00 00 00                                        file_count
0008  33 2E 31 31                                        version = "3.11"
000C  00 00 00 00                                        variant = 0

0010  ... 16 bytes name1 (reversed ASCII)
0020  ... 16 bytes name2 (reversed ASCII)
0030  00 00 00 00  rgcn                                  unk=0, type_tag = NCGR (reversed)
0038  XX XX XX XX  XX XX XX XX                           length, data_offset
... next 48-byte entry ...`}</code></pre>

  <h2>Source</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>notes/asset_extraction_methodology.md</code> — RESC vs RESO layouts</li>
    <li><code>src/translator/_sprite_assoc.py</code> — scanner that treats RESC like RESO</li>
  </ul>
</FieldGuideLayout>
